Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: start a ready source when autoplay is enabled

SetAutoPlay only stored a flag. Load already consumes that flag through Play,
but enabling it after source loading never starts an idle presentation.
Reuse the existing Play path, as original Proton-RTSP does for an idle source.
Do not issue another Play when the latest playback intent is already true.
Store the property before Play can call the application back, so a reentrant
setter wins instead of being overwritten by this older call. Propagate Play
errors without rolling back the property. This differs deliberately from the
original setter's post-Play property assignment.

This deliberately does not add autoplay intent to asynchronous load
completion: that requires reconciling enable/disable with the latest explicit
Play/Pause command. Pending-load toggles remain flag-only; Load still honors
the flag. No new state machine, source-generation rule or automatic retry.
Apply after SE1; independent of the other parity proposals. Source/model
coverage is not a Windows MediaEngine or VRChat playback result.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -3158,14 +3158,19 @@
 static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_SetAutoPlay(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface, BOOL autoplay)
 {
     struct media_engine *engine = impl_from_IMFMediaEngineEx(iface);
+    HRESULT hr = S_OK;
 
-    FIXME("(%p, %d): stub.\n", iface, autoplay);
+    TRACE("%p, %d.\n", iface, autoplay);
 
     EnterCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
     media_engine_set_flag(engine, FLAGS_ENGINE_AUTO_PLAY, autoplay);
+    if (autoplay && !(engine->flags & FLAGS_ENGINE_SHUT_DOWN)
+            && engine->network_state == MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_NETWORK_IDLE
+            && !engine->playback_requested)
+        hr = IMFMediaEngineEx_Play(iface);
     LeaveCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
 
-    return S_OK;
+    return hr;
 }
 
 static BOOL WINAPI media_engine_GetLoop(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface)
